hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"21450","Yahya ibn Saeed narrated to us from Humayd from Anas from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Nothing scratched in my chest since I submitted except that I recited a verse and a man recited other than my recitation, so we came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I said: Did you teach me such and such a verse. He said: Yes. He said: The other said: Did you not teach me such and such a verse. He said: Yes. Jibril came to me upon my right and Mikail upon my left, so Jibril said: Recite the Quran upon one harf, and Mikail said: Ask for more for him, until it reached seven ahruf, each healing, sufficient."
"21451","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Muqaddami narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, saying: Anas said: Ubayy said: Nothing entered my heart since I submitted, and he mentioned the meaning of Ubayy's hadith from Yahya ibn Saeed."
"21452","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Saeed narrated to us: al-Mutamir narrated to us from Humayd from Anas from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: Nothing entered my heart since I submitted, and he mentioned its meaning."
"21453","Abdullah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Makki narrated to us: Abu Damrah narrated to us from Yunus from al-Zuhri from Anas who said: Ubayy used to narrate that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The roof of my house was opened while I was in Makkah, so Jibril descended and opened my chest, then washed it with Zamzam water, then came with a basin of gold filled with wisdom and faith, so he poured it into my chest, then closed it."
